.TP
.B lpui ui
open the keyboard\-driven screen (this runs when you give no command)
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-json
print output as JSON so scripts and agents can read it
.RE
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-version
print the installed version and exit
.RE
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-actor NAME
who made this change (you see it in feed)
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
lpui                             # open the screen (same as `lpui ui`)
lpui list                        # show everything as a tree
lpui list --status doing
lpui show --kind plan --id 1
lpui --actor alice add-plan --title \(dqAPI v2\(dq --why \(dq..\(dq
lpui --actor alice add-criteria --kind plan --id 1 --text \(dqWorks offline\(dq
lpui --actor alice add-task --milestone 1 --title \(dqFix bug\(dq
lpui status --kind task --id 3 --to done
lpui upgrade --check
lpui feed --limit 20
lpui export --format json > backup.json
lpui import --file backup.json
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LAZYPLAN_DB
Which database file to use (same as \fB\-\-db\fR).
.TP
.B USER
Used for \fB\-\-actor\fR when you do not give one.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.lazyplan/lazyplan.db
Your plans, shared by every agent and folder (default home).
.TP
.B .agents/lazyplan/lazyplan.db
The repo database (only with \fBlpui setup \-\-placement repo\fR; commit the config and templates, keep the database local).
.TP
.B ~/.lazyplan/setup.json
Remembered setup choices and migration decisions.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
It worked.
.TP
.B 1
The id you gave was not found (for example, task #7).
.TP
.B 2
The flags or input were wrong (details start with error: ... on stderr).
.TP
.B 3
The screen cannot start (Textual is not installed).
